{"eventType":"response","ts":1767092360054,"jobId":65,"variant":1,"provider":"openai","response":"{ \"en\": { \"description\": \"Company XYZ is a tech company that specializes in developing innovative software solutions to enhance business operations. Founded in 2010, the company has rapidly grown to establish its presence in over 15 countries with a workforce exceeding 1,000 employees. Known for its expertise in cloud computing and AI-driven applications, Company XYZ fosters a culture of innovation and agility, with a mission to empower businesses through cutting-edge technology. However, Company XYZ recently faced operational challenges related to system performance and scalability. Frequent system outages and performance degradation have impacted their system availability, currently at 95%, below the industry standard of 99.9%. The Full Stack Developer role is critical in addressing these issues, focusing on enhancing application performance, reducing latency, and improving deployment frequency, currently at twice a week, to meet the target of daily deployments.\", \"instructions\": \"As the Full Stack Developer at Company XYZ, you are tasked with improving the system's performance and scalability. Your specific objectives include increasing system availability to 99.9%, optimizing application speed, and enhancing deployment frequency to daily releases. Success will involve identifying and resolving current bottlenecks, improving test coverage from 70% to 90%, and collaborating with cross-functional teams to implement CI/CD practices. Constraints include a limited budget and the need to maintain current operations without downtime. Stakeholders expect a comprehensive plan within three weeks and initial performance improvements within two months. Your deliverables include a detailed project plan, weekly progress reports, and a final performance assessment.\", \"questions\": [ \"What immediate steps would you take to assess and address the current system outages im